  "problem": "A volleyball school for children splits the players into three teams, team $1,$ team $2,$ and team $3.$\n\n- $54%$ of the children are in team $1,$ and $20%$ of players in this team have been playing volleyball for over a year.\n\n- $32%$ of the children are in team $2,$ and $30%$ of players in this team have been playing volleyball for over a year.\n\n- $14%$ of the children are in team $3,$ and $15%$ of players in this team have been playing volleyball for over a year.\n\nIf $10%$ of the children can play in all positions, and $94%$ of children that can play in all positions have been playing for over a year, what is the probability that a randomly chosen child who has been playing for over a year can play in all positions? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
